PARITY_COVERED=45
================================================================================

panel map    : the 9 manifest panels = 4 web <MetricCard> tiles (named Avg-Drain-Rate / Total-Phantom-Loss /
               Worst-Session / Drain-Score) + 5 web <GlassPanel> usages (anonymous -> GlassPanel5 gauge L180,
               GlassPanel6 trend L195, GlassPanel7 daily L216, GlassPanel8 sessions L239, GlassPanel9 tips L261).
               All 4 MetricCards always render (0/em-dash before data) and every panel always shows -> no hidden
               sections (ADR-011 #6). The optional web AIVampireDrainExplanation narrator is conditionally null
               (withAiFeature) and never a deterministic panel, so it is not a parity unit (out of scope).
charts       : 3 native chart wrappers, never a webview — RadialGauge (Compose canvas) swept to drain_score colored
               by the score health tier (web scoreColor good/fair/poor -> theme status colors); LineChartWrapper
               (Vico) for the per-session drain-rate trend; BarChartWrapper (Vico) for the per-day drain% + parked
               hours. The web dual-y-axis bar collapses to one Vico axis (exact figures in the accessible data
               table) — an accepted A3 platform adaptation.
states       : the single stats feed drives loading(PageLoader)/error(ErrorDisplay+retry)/success(panels). Within
               success each chart shows its own empty surface (ChartStatus.Empty) and the table its emptyText, so
               loading/empty/error are all implemented and no region is ever blank (ADR-011). isEmpty={false} keeps
               zero/empty stats as content so the panels always render with internal empty surfaces (web parity).
units        : drain rate %/hr, drain %, battery % and the legacy total_energy_lost kWh render verbatim — the
               /vampire-drain/stats endpoint is non-SI percentages + a legacy kWh figure, so no SI scaling applies,
               exactly like the web fmtNumber (unit-conversion.instructions; only locale grouping is applied).
i18n         : every visible literal via stringResource (ADR-014); web key names kept. 8 keys reuse the generated
               res/values catalog (translation_Date/Duration/Sentry/sessions/Score/On/Off + translation_vampire_title
               for vampire.title); the remaining literal-key labels (web i18next-fallback-only, absent from
               web/src/i18n/*.json) live in the app-owned res/values/vampire_drain_strings.xml, English-only so ar/he
               fall back to values/ — reproducing the web's missing-key fallback in every locale (preset_gallery
               precedent). lint MissingTranslation/ExtraTranslation disabled (app/build.gradle.kts L114).
a11y         : Compose semantics paneTitle for the screen title (vampire.title), accessibleDescription on both
               charts + the RadialGauge component description, >=48dp Material 3 targets, dynamic-color + dark theme
               via MaterialTheme tokens; no hardcoded colors/typography (ADR-005/ADR-015).
nav          : Destinations 'vampireDrain' -> /vampire-drain pre-existing (Destinations.kt L85, count unchanged);
               RouteTable already maps the alias /charging/vampire-drain -> vampireDrain (RouteTableTest L163). Host
               wired via PageHosts.register("vampireDrain") in TeslaSyncApplication.onCreate; deep links
               auto-registered by the NavHost. DataContainer untouched (EnergyStore/SettingsStore/SelectedVehicleStore
               already wired).
